<link rel="stylesheet" href="/public/css/sections/nature.css">

<section class="nature-page">
    <section class="nature-hero">
        <div class="nature-hero-overlay">
            <h1>Natural Geography of Malaysia</h1>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="nature-core">
        <div class="container">
            <section class="total-area-row">
                <article class="total-copy">
                    <h2>Total Area</h2>
                    <p>Malaysia has a total land area of approximately 330,803 square kilometers.</p>
                    <p>The country is divided into two main regions:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Peninsular Malaysia (West Malaysia)</li>
                        <li>East Malaysia (Sabah and Sarawak on the island of Borneo)</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>These two regions are separated by the South China Sea.</p>
                </article>
                <figure class="total-photo">
                    <img src="/public/images/langkawi.jpg" alt="Natural area in Malaysia">
                    <figcaption>330,803 km2</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </section>

            <section class="boundaries-row">
                <article class="map-block">
                    <div class="map-image">
                        <iframe src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d16253152.010793893!2d99.1350961745136!3d5.987208086975549!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3034d3975f6730af%3A0x745969328211cd8!2sMalaysia!5e0!3m2!1sid!2sid!4v1773075816607!5m2!1sid!2sid" width="600" height="450" style="border:0;" allowfullscreen="" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
                    </div>
                    <h3><span class="diamond">&#9670;</span> Airspace Boundaries</h3>
                    <p>Malaysia's airspace covers the area above its land and territorial waters in accordance with international aviation law and national sovereignty regulations.</p>
                </article>

                <article class="territorial-block">
                    <h2>Territorial Boundaries</h2>
                    <div class="boundary-group">
                        <h3><span class="diamond">&#9670;</span> Land Borders</h3>
                        <p>Malaysia shares land borders with:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Thailand (north of Peninsular Malaysia)</li>
                            <li>Indonesia (on the island of Borneo)</li>
                            <li>Brunei Darussalam (within Sarawak, East Malaysia)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="boundary-group">
                        <h3><span class="diamond">&#9670;</span> Maritime Borders</h3>
                        <p>Malaysia shares maritime boundaries with:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Indonesia</li>
                            <li>Singapore</li>
                            <li>Philippines</li>
                            <li>Vietnam</li>
                            <li>Thailand</li>
                            <li>Brunei</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="geo-heading-strip">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Geographical Location</h2>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="geo-location">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="location-cards">
                <article class="location-card">
                    <h3>Geographical Position</h3>
                    <p>Malaysia is located in Southeast Asia, strategically positioned along major international trade routes. It is divided into Peninsular Malaysia and East Malaysia on Borneo island.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="location-card">
                    <h3>Geological Position</h3>
                    <p>Geologically, Malaysia lies in a stable plate region. The country has varied landscapes including mountains, rainforests, and coastal plains.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Titiwangsa mountain range</li>
                        <li>Alluvial plains</li>
                        <li>Extensive tropical rainforest</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="location-card">
                    <h3>Astronomical Location</h3>
                    <p>Malaysia lies between 1N to 7N latitude and 100E to 119E longitude, resulting in a tropical climate with warm temperatures throughout the year.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container">
        <section class="landforms">
            <h2>Landforms</h2>
            <div class="landform-grid">
                <article class="landform-card">
                    <img src="/public/images/landform1.png" alt="Mountain range in Malaysia">
                    <h3>Mountains and Mountain Ranges</h3>
                    <p>Malaysia includes several important mountain systems including the Titiwangsa Range and Mount Kinabalu.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="landform-card">
                    <img src="/public/images/landform2.png" alt="Hill and upland in Malaysia">
                    <h3>Hills and Uplands</h3>
                    <p>Much of Peninsular Malaysia consists of rolling hills and uplands, with fertile areas suitable for agriculture and local settlement.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="landform-card">
                    <img src="/public/images/landform3.png" alt="Highlands in Malaysia">
                    <h3>Highlands</h3>
                    <p>Famous highland regions include Cameron Highlands and Genting Highlands, known for cool climate, tourism, and tea plantations.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="landform-card">
                    <img src="/public/images/landform4.png" alt="Lowlands in Malaysia">
                    <h3>Lowlands</h3>
                    <p>Lowland regions are mainly found in coastal zones and river basins, with major population centers and agricultural activity.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <section class="climate-strip">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Airspace Boundaries</h2>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="climate-infographic">
        <div class="container">
            <figure class="climate-card">
                <img src="/public/images/infografis climate.jpeg" alt="Malaysian climate character infographic">
                <figcaption>Seasonal climate patterns across Malaysia</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>